# tools/ales_pan_witness.rish — pan: one mono track placed across a stereo field, opening the second channel (ALES10).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES10.
# Design read: active-designing/20260814-fill-ales10-lotus-pan-stereo.md
# Stands on: lotus/fader.rye (ALES8) — a panned track is TWO faded contributions, so each channel is fader.render run once
# over a pan-folded effective fader; lotus/track.rye (ALES6) — the Session the pans align with; lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2) —
# the Clip and the one true saturation, reached through ALES8.
#
# lotus/pan.rye opens the second channel with the simplest honest law — a LINEAR pan, a track's level split between left and
# right by weights that sum to one. Pan is a pure fraction fold into the fader, so the only sum in the suite stays ALES8's,
# run once per channel. Its defining invariant is that adding the two channels reproduces the mono mix EXACTLY, for any pan
# position. The selftest proves: center pan splits equally; hard left/right route wholly; pan composes with the fader; two
# tracks panned opposite separate; left + right == the mono mix for any pan (in-range); make refuses BadGain/BadRange; a
# track past the master bound forwards ClipFull. Purely local — no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_pan_witness.rish

say "ales-pan: Language EN — ALES10 opens the second channel: pan places each mono track somewhere between the left and right speaker, the first stereo gesture."
say "ales-pan: Style Radiant — the linear pan splits a level by weights that sum to one, and its invariant is stated positively: left + right reproduces the mono mix exactly, for any pan position."
say "ales-pan: Lens TAME — pan is a bounded fraction fold into the fader (weights and denominators within max_pan_den, asserted so no product overflows), each channel ALES8's fader.render run once; refuses BadGain / BadRange / ClipFull by name; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/pan"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/pan.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-pan: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/pan.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-pan: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-pan: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-pan' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-pan: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-pan line"

say "ales-pan: GREEN — pan opens the stereo field as a pure fraction fold, left + right reproducing the mono mix for any pan; each channel is ALES8's one sum run once. The next Lotus rung can name a stereo balance/width control, a transport loop over a marked region, or the equal-power crossfade curve."
